+      <h1 id="page-title">Cat FAQ</h1>
+      <p class="intro">Quick answers for curious cat people, from purring and playtime to feeding, grooming, and keeping indoor cats enriched.</p>
+    </section>
+
+    <section class="faq" aria-label="Frequently asked questions about cats">
+      <div class="example">
+        <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="answer-1" id="question-1">
+          Why do cats purr?
+          <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
+        </button>
+        <div class="details" id="answer-1" role="region" aria-labelledby="question-1" aria-hidden="true">
+          <div class="details-inner">
+            <p>Cats often purr when they feel comfortable, but purring can also happen when they are stressed, injured, or self-soothing. Context matters: a relaxed body, slow blinking, and gentle kneading usually point to contentment.</p>
+          </div>
+        </div>
+      </div>
+
+      <div class="example">
+        <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="answer-2" id="question-2">
+          How much sleep do cats need?
+          <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
+        </button>
+        <div class="details" id="answer-2" role="region" aria-labelledby="question-2" aria-hidden="true">
+          <div class="details-inner">
+            <p>Most adult cats sleep around <strong>12 to 16 hours a day</strong>, while kittens and senior cats may sleep even more. Short bursts of activity at dawn and dusk are normal because cats are naturally crepuscular.</p>
+          </div>
+        </div>
+      </div>
+
+      <div class="example">
+        <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="answer-3" id="question-3">
+          Why does my cat knead blankets or people?
+          <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
+        </button>
+        <div class="details" id="answer-3" role="region" aria-labelledby="question-3" aria-hidden="true">
+          <div class="details-inner">
+            <p>Kneading is a kitten behavior that many cats keep into adulthood. It can signal comfort, bonding, or a desire to make a resting spot feel just right. Keeping claws trimmed helps make kneading less prickly.</p>
+          </div>
+        </div>
+      </div>
+
+      <div class="example">
+        <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="answer-4" id="question-4">
+          How often should cats be groomed?
+          <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
+        </button>
+        <div class="details" id="answer-4" role="region" aria-labelledby="question-4" aria-hidden="true">
+          <div class="details-inner">
+            <p>Short-haired cats usually benefit from weekly brushing, while long-haired cats may need brushing several times a week or daily. Regular grooming reduces shedding, prevents mats, and gives you a chance to notice skin or coat changes.</p>
+          </div>
+        </div>
+      </div>
+
+      <div class="example">
+        <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="answer-5" id="question-5">
+          What should indoor cats do for enrichment?
+          <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
+        </button>
+        <div class="details" id="answer-5" role="region" aria-labelledby="question-5" aria-hidden="true">
+          <div class="details-inner">
+            <p>Indoor cats thrive with climbing spaces, scratching posts, puzzle feeders, window perches, and daily interactive play. Rotate toys to keep them novel, and end play sessions with a small meal or treat to mimic a hunt-catch-eat rhythm.</p>
+          </div>
+        </div>
+      </div>
+
+      <div class="example">
+        <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="answer-6" id="question-6">
+          How much water should a cat drink?
+          <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
+        </button>
+        <div class="details" id="answer-6" role="region" aria-labelledby="question-6" aria-hidden="true">
+          <div class="details-inner">
+            <p>Water needs vary with diet, activity, weather, and health. Wet food adds meaningful moisture, while fountains and wide bowls can encourage drinking. Sudden changes in thirst or urination are worth discussing with a veterinarian.</p>
+          </div>
+        </div>
+      </div>
+    </section>
+  </main>
+
+  <script>
+    const questions = document.querySelectorAll(".question");
+
+    questions.forEach((question) => {
+      question.addEventListener("click", () => {
+        const answer = document.getElementById(question.getAttribute("aria-controls"));
+        const isExpanded = question.getAttribute("aria-expanded") === "true";
+
+        question.setAttribute("aria-expanded", String(!isExpanded));
+        answer.setAttribute("aria-hidden", String(isExpanded));
+      });
+    });
+  </script>
+</body>
+</html>
*** End Patch
